@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title The prompt kit — what `proveo init` installs so the shell prompt can show what runs left
' purpose: what the prompt row of `proveo init` installs, how each download is verified, and what `proveo uninstall` takes back
' covers: internal/promptkit/pins.go
' covers: internal/promptkit/fetch.go
' covers: internal/promptkit/install.go
' covers: internal/promptkit/segment.go
' covers: internal/promptkit/kit.go
' covers: internal/promptkit/promptkit_test.go
' covers: internal/promptkit/gate_test.go
' covers: internal/shell/shell.go (PromptMarker, StarshipLine, PromptBlock, StartsStarship, WithoutPromptBlock)
' covers: internal/choiceui/glyphs_dialog.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/init_prompt.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/init_prompt_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/init_tui.go (rowPrompt)
' covers: cmd/proveo/prompt.go (--init)
' covers: cmd/proveo/uninstall.go (promptkit.Undo)
'   why a prompt segment at all ...... _spec/internal/results/result-store.puml (D4)
'   what the segment prints .......... _spec/internal/results/result-store.puml
'   the order it landed in ........... _spec/_plans/tui-upgrades-delivery.puml (W8)
'   the other block init writes ...... _spec/internal/shell/setup-path.puml
'   the dialog it asks with .......... _spec/internal/choiceui/confirm-dialogs.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT WAS DECIDED ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' The Executor, 2026-11-10: "There is already a post-install `proveo` script
' that installs `sbx`. `starship` should be installed along" (D13), and "Let
' the post-install download FiraCode Nerd Font if no nerd font is present in
' the host at install time" (D14), from the .zip (D18: "The .zip, 27 MB").
' So `proveo init` gains one row, "prompt", now or later, and `--skip-prompt`.
' Its help line says the cost: starship REPLACES the shell's whole prompt.
'
' ── THE FOUR STEPS (promptkit.Apply) ───────────────────────────────────────
'   starship   only when none is on PATH. The pinned v1.27.0 archive for the
'              host lands beside proveo's own binary.
'   the font   only when the host has NO Nerd Font. FiraCode Nerd Font
'              (Nerd Fonts v3.5.1, FiraCode.zip) is unpacked into the
'              per-user font directory.
'   the shell  only when the rc file does not already start starship. One
'              marked block is appended: bash and zsh get `eval "$(starship
'              init <shell>)"`, fish gets `starship init fish | source`.
'   the block  one fenced `[custom.proveo]` block in starship's config
'              (STARSHIP_CONFIG, else ~/.config/starship.toml).
' Each step says what it did, or that the host already had it. A second
' Apply downloads nothing and adds nothing.
' HOW IT SAYS SO (R3 of _spec/_plans/output-readability.puml, 2026-11-11).
' Options.Fact and Options.Warn carry everything Apply and Undo say; R4 deleted
' Options.Report and its sentences, since init had set it to nil and uninstall
' now prints facts too. Undo says each removal that SUCCEEDED as a fact, "rc",
' "config", "starship" or "font" (FontFamily, dim "<n> files in <dir>", n the
' files it removed), and each that failed as a Warn ("<config> — proveo
' segment not removed", the error dim); the error it returns joins those. It
' used to say "removed the proveo segment from <config>" before it checked the
' write (FOUND 3, MEASURED: a read-only ~/.config). Installed asks Undo's
' own checks, so `proveo uninstall` names "the prompt kit" in its question only
' when Undo has something to remove (_spec/internal/shell/setup-path.puml).
' Pinned by TestUndoSaysOnlyWhatItRemoved and, in cmd/proveo,
' TestUninstallTakesThePromptKitOutAndLeavesTheOperatorsConfig. init prints
' ONE block under "prompt" from Apply's:
'   starship  <version> + dim "installed at ~/…", or <path> + "already on PATH"
'   font      FiraCode Nerd Font + dim "<n> files in ~/…", or "a Nerd Font"
'             + "already installed"
'   rc        <rc> + dim "added `<line>`" or "already starts starship"
'   config    <config> + dim "created from starship's <preset> preset",
'             "holds the proveo segment"
'   ⚠ <shell> — no starship line known, dim "start starship from its
'             startup file yourself" (a degrade the operator did not cause)
'   ⚠ prompt kit — not finished, its error dim
' "open a new shell to see it; `proveo uninstall` takes it out again" and
' "to see icons, set your terminal's font …, then `starship preset …`" moved
' to `proveo init --help` (F2). NOT CHOSEN: routing Report to ui.Logf (init
' writes no log, so the lines would land nowhere). Pinned by internal/promptkit/promptkit_test.go
' TestApplySaysWhatItFoundAsFactsAndAShellWithNoLineAsAWarning.
'
' ── EVERY DOWNLOAD IS HELD TO A DIGEST IN THE SOURCE ───────────────────────
' The plan said "checked against its published .sha256". The digests are
' pinned in pins.go instead, read from the publishers' own files on
' 2026-11-11: starship's six `<asset>.sha256` files and Nerd Fonts'
' SHA-256.txt. A release edited after that day no longer matches, where a
' digest fetched beside the archive would follow the edit.
' MEASURED 2026-11-11: starship-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz hashed to its
' published digest and holds one file, `starship`. FiraCode.zip is
' 28,602,426 bytes, hashed to its published digest, and holds 18 font files,
' a LICENSE and a README.
' A body whose sha256 differs is refused and nothing is written. Downloads
' are capped at 96 MB and five minutes.
' The archive entries are written by BASE NAME into one directory: an entry
' named `../../x.ttf` lands inside the font directory as `x.ttf`.
' Only `.ttf` and `.otf` entries are unpacked.
'
' ── "HAS A NERD FONT" IS A FILE NAME ───────────────────────────────────────
' A font file (.ttf, .otf, .ttc) whose name holds "NerdFont" or "Nerd Font",
' at any depth of the user and system font directories:
'   darwin   ~/Library/Fonts, /Library/Fonts, /System/Library/Fonts
'   linux    $XDG_DATA_HOME/fonts (~/.local/share/fonts), ~/.fonts,
'            /usr/local/share/fonts, /usr/share/fonts
'   windows  %LOCALAPPDATA%\Microsoft\Windows\Fonts, %WINDIR%\Fonts
' [Unverified] The Linux and Windows directories were written from their
' conventions; only the macOS scan ran against a real font.
' [Unverified] No font cache is refreshed on Linux (`fc-cache`).
'
' ── INSTALLED IS NOT ENABLED, SO INIT ASKS ─────────────────────────────────
' This host has FiraCode Nerd Font installed and no terminal set to use it.
' proveo cannot ask a terminal what it draws. When Apply CREATES starship's
' config on a headed terminal, a button dialog shows two Nerd glyphs, the
' branch U+F418 and the lock U+F033E, and asks what was drawn:
'   Something else (the safe answer, selected)   seeds starship's
'                  `no-nerd-font` preset and prints the font to set in the
'                  terminal
'   Two icons      seeds its `nerd-font-symbols` preset
' The text counts anything but two icons as "no": a box, a question mark, a
' line, a blank, or one icon of the two.
' With --yes, without a terminal, or when the config already exists, nothing
' is asked: a new config gets `no-nerd-font`.
' MEASURED 2026-11-11: the probe drew U+E0A0, the Powerline branch. The
' `nerd-font-symbols` preset of starship 1.27.0 holds 128 private-use glyphs
' and U+E0A0 is not one of them; its git branch is U+F418. An operator on
' this host saw "a line", which the old text ("an empty box or a question
' mark") did not name.
' [Inference] A terminal that draws Powerline glyphs itself passed the old
' probe without a Nerd Font.
' DECIDED 2026-11-11 (Executor: "Preset glyphs + reword"): both glyphs come
' from the preset. U+F033E, the preset's read-only lock, sits in plane 15,
' so the probe also covers the preset's glyphs outside the BMP.
' AN EXISTING CONFIG GAINS THE BLOCK AND NOTHING ELSE. No preset is applied to
' a file the operator wrote; its mode is kept.
'
' ── THE BLOCK ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   [custom.proveo]
'   command = "proveo prompt"
'   when = true                         a custom module defaults to never
'   require_repo = true                 nothing outside a repository
'   format = "[($output )]($style)"     nothing when the command prints nothing
' It is fenced by two comment lines, so WithSegment replaces an edited block
' in place and WithoutSegment gives the file back byte for byte.
' MEASURED with starship 1.27.0 over this block: in a repository it drew
' "1 kept · 2 to adopt"; outside one it drew nothing; with `proveo prompt`
' printing nothing it drew nothing.
' [Inference] An operator whose own `format` leaves out `$custom` will not
' see the module; the block does not edit their format.
'
' ── WHAT UNINSTALL TAKES BACK ──────────────────────────────────────────────
' Apply records what proveo itself installed in <state>/prompt-kit.json.
' `proveo uninstall` removes the marked rc block and the fenced config block
' always, and the starship binary and the font files ONLY when the record
' names them. A `starship init` line the operator wrote stays; so does a
' starship they installed and a Nerd Font they had.
' `proveo prompt --init <shell>` prints the one line for bash, zsh or fish,
' for an operator who would rather add it by hand.
' NOT DONE: a real `proveo init` with the prompt row on this host. It would
' edit the operator's rc file and starship config; that waits for them.
' [Unverified] Windows: starship has a build, but internal/shell writes no
' PowerShell line, so the rc step reports that and does nothing.
'
' Pinned by internal/promptkit/promptkit_test.go:
'   TestThePinsNameOneAssetAndOneDigestPerHost
'   TestInstallStarshipRefusesAnArchiveThatIsNotThePinnedOne
'   TestANerdFontIsRecognisedByItsFileName
'   TestInstallFontWritesOnlyFontFilesAndOnlyInsideTheDirectory
'   TestTheSegmentIsAddedOnceAndNothingElseChanges
'   TestApplyOnAnEmptyHostInstallsEverythingAndUndoRemovesIt
'   TestApplyOnAHostThatHasItAllAddsOnlyTheSegment
'   TestUndoSaysOnlyWhatItRemoved
'   TestTheGlyphAnswerPicksThePreset
' by internal/promptkit/gate_test.go, against the real tools when installed:
'   TestEachShellParsesTheBlockProveoAppends (bash -n, zsh -n, fish --no-execute)
'   TestStarshipDrawsTheSegmentInARepositoryAndNothingOutsideOne
' by internal/shell: TestTheStarshipLineIsEachShellsOwnAndItsBlockComesOutClean
' and by cmd/proveo/init_prompt_test.go:
'   TestThePromptRowDefaultsToNowAndSkipPromptLocksItOff
' and by internal/choiceui/dialog_test.go:
'   TestTheGlyphProbeDrawsThePresetsBranchAndLockAndCountsAnythingElseAsNo
'   TestPromptInitPrintsEachShellsLineAndRefusesAnUnknownShell
'   TestUninstallTakesThePromptKitOutAndLeavesTheOperatorsConfig

component """proveo init""\nthe prompt row: now · later" as INIT <<app>>
component "starship v1.27.0\nonly when none is on PATH" as STAR <<cloud>>
component "FiraCode Nerd Font v3.5.1\nonly when the host has none" as FONT <<cloud>>
component "the shell's rc file\none marked block" as RC <<host>>
component "starship's config\none fenced ""[custom.proveo]"" block" as CFG <<host>>
database """prompt-kit.json""\nwhat proveo itself installed" as REC <<db>>
component "**a download that is not the pinned one**\nrefused, nothing written" as BAD <<error>>
component """proveo uninstall""" as UN <<app>>

INIT ARROW_MAIN STAR
INIT ARROW_MAIN FONT
INIT ARROW_MAIN RC
INIT ARROW_MAIN CFG
INIT ARROW_MAIN REC
BAD ARROW_ERROR STAR : sha256 pinned in the source
BAD ARROW_ERROR FONT
UN ARROW_OPTIONAL REC : removes what it names, and the two blocks

note bottom of STAR
  **Held to a digest in the source.** The six
  starship digests and the font's were read
  from the publishers' files once and pinned.
  A changed release no longer installs.
end note

note bottom of FONT
  **Installed is not enabled.** A terminal may
  not use the font it has. Init shows one
  glyph and asks; the safe answer is the
  preset that needs no Nerd Font.
end note

note bottom of CFG
  **One fenced block, and nothing else.** An
  existing config keeps every line and its
  mode. The block comes out again byte for
  byte.
end note

note bottom of REC
  **Uninstall takes back what init brought.**
  The binary and the font files go only when
  the record names them. The operator's own
  starship, font and init line stay.
end note
@enduml
